QEMU40PAD-AD — synthetic 5D4 EDID through natural CH2 slave 0x7C
========================================================================

Classification: RESEARCH UPDATE / QEMU-VERIFIED EXPERIMENT
Target firmware: Canon EOS 5D Mark IV 1.3.3
Physical-camera validation: none

Experimental baseline hw/eos/eos.c SHA-256:
809da93ab66fa1bfde796950126b839627e9b95b7f90e4d54135da5dd4fa166e

Result hw/eos/eos.c SHA-256:
31f5aa4220c415a8df3c6eddcfd119a17b27815964037f5cf6770a6d3c4e3a1d

Original workcard patch SHA-256:
25037ffa8b55c292c4753dea230ebb805e71bda64b2089cb9dd3eb4e8ae0fe19

This incremental patch depends on the accumulated PAD-U/PAD-AD experimental
baseline; it is not directly applicable to upstream qemu-eos 4b667a1d.

The EDID is a deliberately minimal checksum-valid synthetic witness. It does
not model a real connected monitor. Verbose PAD-AD logging is retained because
it was present in the runtime-validated source; cleanup requires a separate
build/runtime checkpoint.

